  "change": "Add a pinned notify-based vault watcher with coalesced invalidation hints, overflow and root replacement recovery, and periodic disk reconciliation after sleep or missed notifications.",
  "focused_test": {
    "name": "egui_reconciles_from_disk_after_a_sleep_or_reconnect_gap",
    "command": "cargo test --workspace --locked",
    "result": "Passed on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows GitHub Actions jobs.",
    "related_watcher_tests": [
      "watcher::tests::overflow_event_requires_a_disk_rescan_even_without_paths",
      "watcher::tests::reconnect_after_root_replacement_rearms_watch_and_rescans_disk",
      "watcher::tests::relevant_file_events_are_hints_without_becoming_authoritative_state"
    ]
  },
  "scenario_result": [
    "The watcher recovery fixture covers overflow, sleep or missed notifications, and root reconnect; reconciliation reads the vault from disk and does not trust event payloads as state.",
    "The egui sleep/reconnect case found the externally added note after periodic reconciliation and verified its exact CRLF source bytes.",
    "A first exact-SHA CI attempt exposed a timing-only test assertion: a fast refresh could complete and clear its receiver in the first UI frame. The final test accepts an active receiver or the completed refresh status, then verifies the note was reconciled."
  ],
